import{_ as s,o as t,c as o,ag as n}from"./chunks/framework.-5_vvMqw.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"The Workspace view","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"workspace.md","filePath":"workspace.md","lastUpdated":1794043946000}'),a={name:"workspace.md"};function r(i,e,h,l,d,g){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="the-workspace-view" tabindex="-1">The Workspace view <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-workspace-view" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Workspace view&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The Workspace shows an interactive session&#39;s conversation as a chat: what you asked, what the agent answered, and a compact log of the tools it used. Next to it you can open the session&#39;s files, the Changes view and the integrated browser, and a terminal drawer when you need the agent&#39;s own console.</p><p><strong>Edition:</strong> Community · <strong>Who:</strong> the session owner. A Collaborator on a <a href="/docs/sharing">shared session</a> (Enterprise) can read and write messages too; a Viewer can only read.</p><h2 id="workspace-or-terminal" tabindex="-1">Workspace or Terminal <a class="header-anchor" href="#workspace-or-terminal" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Workspace or Terminal&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each session opens in one of two interfaces, chosen under <strong>Interface</strong> when you create it:</p><ul><li><strong>Workspace</strong>: conversation, tasks and tools in one view.</li><li><strong>Terminal</strong>: the agent CLI&#39;s own console interface.</li></ul><p>The default for new sessions is set per browser under <strong>Settings → Interface</strong>. You can switch a running session between the two with the <strong>Workspace</strong> and <strong>Terminal</strong> buttons in its header, without restarting the agent.</p><p>In the Workspace, <strong>⌘ Agent terminal</strong> opens the agent&#39;s console in a drawer below the conversation, and <strong>›_ Shell</strong> opens a separate shell in the session&#39;s container. The shell is only offered to the session owner.</p><h2 id="the-conversation" tabindex="-1">The conversation <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-conversation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The conversation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>New messages appear live while the agent works. Long conversations open with the most recent part; <strong>Load earlier messages</strong> goes further back.</li><li><strong>Find in conversation…</strong> searches the messages that are loaded.</li><li>Each message has <strong>Copy</strong> and <strong>Quote</strong> actions; <strong>Quote</strong> puts the text into your draft.</li><li>Hover a time stamp for the full date and time.</li><li>The conversation survives a pause, a restart and a runtime update, and it follows the agent&#39;s <code>/clear</code> and <code>/new</code>.</li><li>Long links and inline code wrap; code blocks and tables scroll on their own.</li></ul><h2 id="opencode-conversations" tabindex="-1">OpenCode conversations <a class="header-anchor" href="#opencode-conversations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;OpenCode conversations&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Choose <strong>OpenCode</strong> and <strong>Workspace</strong> when creating a session, or switch an existing OpenCode session to Workspace from its header. The conversation shows your messages, completed answers, tool calls and tool results from OpenCode&#39;s own history. Open <strong>Agent terminal</strong> for the CLI&#39;s menus, login and an answer while it is still streaming.</p><p>Earlier messages remain available after reconnecting; use <strong>Load earlier messages</strong> in a long conversation. History catches up in bounded pages. A message appears after OpenCode has saved it; answers appear when complete. Long text and tool output may be shortened, with an omission notice. Native subagent conversations and reasoning are not shown as separate conversations.</p><p>This is included in <strong>Community Edition</strong> for session owners. With <strong>Enterprise</strong> sharing, Viewers can read the conversation and Collaborators can also send messages, subject to their existing session permissions. Shared reads use the same masking as other session history. OpenCode&#39;s managed tool policy and approval prompts still apply to tools started from the CLI.</p><h2 id="the-composer" tabindex="-1">The composer <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-composer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The composer&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Type in <strong>Give your agent a task…</strong> and press <strong>Enter</strong> to send (<strong>Shift+Enter</strong> for a new line).</p><ul><li><strong>Slash commands:</strong> type <code>/</code> to list the commands of the session&#39;s agent CLI, including custom commands and, where the CLI offers them, skills. Up and Down move the highlight, Tab or Enter complete it, Escape closes the list.</li><li><strong>Suggestions:</strong> when the CLI predicts your next message, it appears greyed out in the input. <strong>→</strong> or <strong>Tab</strong> accepts it into your draft; you still send it yourself. Typing dismisses it.</li><li><strong>Attachments:</strong> paste an image, drop files onto the composer, or use <strong>＋ Attach files</strong>. The files are uploaded to the session&#39;s <a href="/docs/files">files</a> and the agent receives them with your message; images show as thumbnails in the conversation.</li><li><strong>◼ Stop</strong> interrupts the agent&#39;s current turn.</li></ul><p>Your draft is kept per session while you look at another one.</p><h2 id="messages-that-wait" tabindex="-1">Messages that wait <a class="header-anchor" href="#messages-that-wait" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Messages that wait&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When the agent is busy, a message you send is shown as pending until the agent takes it:</p><ul><li><strong>Send now</strong> delivers it into the running turn as a priority message instead of waiting for the turn to end.</li><li><strong>Interrupt and send</strong> stops the agent&#39;s turn, and the agent then takes your message at once.</li><li><strong>✕</strong> stops showing it as pending.</li></ul><p>While the agent is not ready yet (for example while the session is starting), messages go into a queue above the composer, marked <em>Queued · will be sent when the agent is ready</em>. <strong>Edit</strong> puts one back into the composer, <strong>Withdraw</strong> removes it.</p><h2 id="messages-from-other-sessions" tabindex="-1">Messages from other sessions <a class="header-anchor" href="#messages-from-other-sessions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Messages from other sessions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>✉ Messages</strong> button in the session header (owner only) opens a panel with the messages other sessions sent to this one, with a badge for how many are open. <strong>Message this agent</strong> sends your own message; tick <strong>priority</strong> to deliver it into the running prompt now, and <strong>interrupt</strong> to stop the current work first. How sessions message each other is described in <a href="/docs/session-tools">Built-in tools inside a session</a>.</p><h2 id="files-changes-and-the-browser" tabindex="-1">Files, Changes and the browser <a class="header-anchor" href="#files-changes-and-the-browser" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Files, Changes and the browser&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The session bar opens companion panes beside the conversation:</p><ul><li><strong>Files</strong>: the session&#39;s files, with previews. See <a href="/docs/files">Session files</a>.</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>, a view inside the Files pane: a per-file Git diff of the agent&#39;s work in the repositories under the workspace. It needs a running session.</li><li><strong>Browser</strong>: the integrated browser, once the agent has started it. See <a href="/docs/browser">Integrated browser</a>.</li></ul><p>Drag the separator between the conversation and the pane to resize it between 25 % and 75 %; with the keyboard, focus the separator and use the arrow keys. On a phone the panes take turns with the conversation.</p><h2 id="starting-waiting-and-stopped-states" tabindex="-1">Starting, waiting and stopped states <a class="header-anchor" href="#starting-waiting-and-stopped-states" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Starting, waiting and stopped states&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Session starting</strong> shows the stage: waiting for the pod, then starting the agent. It ends when the agent can take input.</li><li>An activity line shows whether the agent is working or waiting for you.</li><li>When the session is paused, finished, failed or scheduled, the composer is replaced by a bar that says so. The owner gets <strong>Resume</strong> there. A finished autonomous run offers to <a href="/docs/sessions#continue-an-autonomous-run-interactively">continue interactively</a>.</li><li>If a CLI needs a sign-in, a sign-in card appears in the conversation; see <a href="/docs/provider-login">Provider login</a>.</li></ul><p>Questions and permission requests from the agent appear in the Workspace as well; see <a href="/docs/questions-approvals">Questions and approvals</a>.</p><h2 id="limits" tabindex="-1">Limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Limits&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The message-by-message conversation is available for Claude, Codex and OpenCode, which keep a native conversation record. For Cursor and OpenClaw the Workspace shows the cleaned terminal history instead, without per-message times; use the Terminal for those agents when you need the full console.</li></ul><h2 id="preparing-a-provider-handover" tabindex="-1">Preparing a provider handover <a class="header-anchor" href="#preparing-a-provider-handover" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Preparing a provider handover&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The upcoming <a href="/docs/handover-preview">handover preview API</a> lets an owner review a bounded text selection. It does not yet switch the running provider or send the text to another agent.</p>',35)])])}const u=s(a,[["render",r]]);export{c as __pageData,u as default};
